  "worked_solution": "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nA\u2227(A\u2228\u00acB)\u2261A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00acB\u2227(A\u2228\u00acB) & \u2261\u00acB\u2227(\u00acB\u2228A) \\\\  & \u2261\u00acB\u2262A.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\u00acB\u2228A)\u2227A & \u2261A\u2227(\u00acB\u2228A) \\\\  & \u2261A\u2227(A\u2228\u00acB) \\\\  & \u2261A.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\u2227(\u00acB\u2228A) & \u2261A\u2227(A\u2228\u00acB) \\\\  & \u2261A.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
